@using Fhi.Munin.Explorer.Blazor
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Utforskeren i helsedatas stiler";
}

@* `container` is the wrapper helsedata's own MuninUtforsker.cshtml puts around the mount, and
   the component is the only thing on the page — no heading, no ingress, no breadcrumb. That is
   deliberate: their Munin page has nothing above the component either, so the component's own
   first element is what meets the header. Adding chrome here would pad the measurement and hide
   the defect this host exists to catch.

   IsAuthenticated is hardcoded true. This host has no sign-in, and with it false there is no
   tablist and no list panel at all — ShowTabs is `VariableList is not null && IsAuthenticated` —
   so three of the four assertions would have nothing to measure and would pass vacuously. *@
<div class="container">
    <component type="typeof(VariableExplorer)"
               render-mode="Server"
               param-Language="@("no")"
               param-IsAuthenticated="@(true)" />
</div>
